THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------
KASA depends on third-party software that is NOT covered by the license above.
Each component remains under its own license and is the property of its own
authors.  A commercial license for KASA grants no rights in these components.

Declared in requirements.txt.  The license identifiers below were read from
installed distribution metadata on the author's machine.  The versions shown are
only the versions that happened to be checked -- they are not pinned
requirements, and they do not all come from one environment: mcp was read from
the Python 3.12 install, the rest from Python 3.14.  The packaging script builds
with Python 3.12 (build_kasa.ps1, lines 30 and 59), where some versions differ.
The license identifiers were the same in both environments; only versions moved.

  fastapi       0.138.0   MIT
  uvicorn       0.48.0    BSD-3-Clause
  pydantic      2.13.4    MIT
  PyQt5         5.15.11   GPL v3
  cryptography  49.0.0    Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause
  mcp           1.28.1    MIT

Note on PyQt5: its metadata declares GPL v3, and its licensor offers a separate
commercial track.  Inside src/ it is imported only by the system-tray helper
(src/tray/app.py); the desktop UI runs on pywebview over WebView2, not Qt.  The
packaging script excludes Qt from the build (build_kasa.ps1, line 62) and does
not package src.tray, so an executable produced by that script does not ship
PyQt5.  Anyone packaging KASA differently, or planning a closed-source product,
must resolve that component's licensing independently -- see COMMERCIAL.md
section 8.

Note on mcp: used only by the src/mcp_adapter stdio process (its sole import in
src/ is src/mcp_adapter/__main__.py, line 35).  It is not bundled into the
packaged executable: the build script's package list does not include
src.mcp_adapter (build_kasa.ps1, lines 70-75), which matches the declaration in
requirements.txt, line 6.

Verify the license of every dependency against the version you actually install.
The list above is a snapshot, not a guarantee.

At runtime on Windows, KASA may additionally require Microsoft WebView2 Runtime
and the Visual C++ Redistributable.  These are Microsoft components under
Microsoft's own terms and are not distributed with KASA (see TERMS_OF_USE.md).


